      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Storing high volumes of flammable industrial solvents in high-density racking systems can be a bit like trying to herd cats, but with a few more fire hazards thrown in for good measure. One of the main issues with these systems is that they can be a bit of a maze, with lots of hidden corners and hard-to-reach areas. This can make it difficult to spot a leak or an ignition point early on, which is a bit like trying to find a needle in a haystack, except the needle is on fire and the haystack is made of flammable solvents.\n\nThe physical layout of the racking system can also play a role in complicating early detection. If the containers are stacked too high or too close together, it can be difficult to see or reach them, especially if they're in a hidden or hard-to-reach area. This can make it difficult to spot a leak or an ignition point, which can lead to a larger fire if not detected early enough.\n\nIn addition, the high-density nature of the racking system can also make it difficult to detect a leak or an ignition point. If the containers are packed too tightly together, it can be difficult to see or feel if there's a leak or an ignition point.",
